Swipe Keyboard licences

Swipe Keyboard follows the REUSE specification (https://reuse.software): every file names its copyright holders and
licence, either in an SPDX header or in REUSE.toml, and the full licence texts are in LICENSES/.

- MIT: the engine (engine/: swipe recognition, dictionary, completion, prediction, learning), tools/, scripts/,
  bench/, the launcher and command-line tool (integration/), the Gaming Mode daemon (gaming/), their tests and all
  CMake build files.
- GPL-2.0-only OR GPL-3.0-only OR LicenseRef-KDE-Accepted-GPL (KDE's standard; you may use the GNU GPL version 2 or
  version 3, or a later version accepted by KDE e.V.): only the keyboard add-on layers, because they plug into GPL
  software and must stay compatible with it: plugin/ (Plasma 6.7/6.8, linked with Qt Virtual Keyboard, GPL-3.0-only)
  and frontend-plasma69/ (Plasma 6.9, runs inside KDE's plasma-keyboard and uses its internals), with their tests.
  The patches to KDE's code in scripts/patches/ keep KDE's licence.
- Documentation and images: CC-BY-4.0. Trivial or generated data: CC0-1.0.
- Data files keep their own licences: word lists and language packs ODC-By-1.0 and CC BY 2.0 France (Tatoeba), the
  AOSP word list Apache-2.0, the swear-word lists CC-BY-4.0, the texting-word lists CC0-1.0, the trained models as
  declared in their release (see packaging/NOTICE and packaging/language-models/README.md).

Note on built programs: the shared language and session rules live in plugin/ (KDE's GPL choice) and are also linked
into the Gaming Mode daemon and some tools, so those binaries as built combine MIT and GPL code and are distributed
under the GPL's terms; their own source files remain MIT.

